Hello there,=0A=0AIn order to properly add support to OpenWrt for the Lin=
ksys WHW01 v1 (FCC ID Q87-0333) [1], BDFs were required to be extracted f=
rom the vendor's firmware (version 1.1.13.202617 [2]). Without these the =
radios did not appear to operate correctly; the 5GHz radio was unable to =
scan, and when running in AP mode, clients were unable to connect.=0A=0AT=
he vendor firmware appears to provide a number of board files which are i=
nstalled at device power-on depending on the configured region - AU, FCC,=
 EU, etc. Only the FCC board files have been included here, as I'm unsure=
 whether all files should be submitted and whether there are any differen=
ces (although their md5s did not match)?=0A=0AInformation requested, per =
the wiki page [3]:=0A=0A* description for what hardware this is:=0A=0A  -=
 it is a IPQ4018 based board=0A    - one qca4019 radio is used as 2.4GHz =
radio=0A    - one qca4019 radio is used as 5GHz radio=0A=0A* origin of th=
e board file (did you create it yourself or where you downloaded)=0A=0A  =
- Extracted from Linksys WHW01 v1 firmware (1.1.13.202617) [2]=0A=0A* ids=
 to be used with the board file (ATH10K_BD_IE_BOARD_NAME in ath10k)=0A=0A=
  - bus=3Dahb,bmi-chip-id=3D0,bmi-board-id=3D16,variant=3Dlinksys-whw01-v=
1=0A    md5: 92f5a223a963211d884b6211385dfa91=0A  - bus=3Dahb,bmi-chip-id=
=3D0,bmi-board-id=3D17,variant=3Dlinksys-whw01-v1=0A    md5: 5bb0357df9cf=
3614fe4d9db696d09e43=0A=0ARegards,=0APeter Adkins=0A=0A[1] https://github=
.com/openwrt/openwrt/pull/3682=0A[2] https://www.linksys.com/us/support-a=
rticle?articleNum=3D226207=0A[3] https://wireless.wiki.kernel.org/en/user=
s/drivers/ath10k/boardfiles

